      {
        "factor": "Active Sabah petition environment (Lamag and Sindumin petitions)",
        "direction": "up",
        "magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "Sabah has active petition activity that raises the possibility of challenge and review, providing upward pressure on overturn risk."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Large Lamag margin reduces overturn likelihood",
        "direction": "down",
        "magnitude": "strong",
        "rationale": "A 5,681-vote majority makes successful overturns substantially less probable, exerting strong downward pressure."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Historical precedents show overturns possible but rare",
        "direction": "down",
        "magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "Few past cases exist (Cameron Highlands, Kimanis) and they are outliers, suggesting low base risk."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Recount threshold (4%) is not satisfied by Lamag margin",
        "direction": "down",
        " magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "Margin far above any automatic recount threshold reduces the likelihood of a reversal via recount."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Timeline uncertainties and court-backlog could delay resolution",
        "direction": "neutral",
        "magnitude": "weak",
        "rationale": "Judicial timelines could push a decision past May 1, 2026, adding uncertainty but not clearly increasing overturn probability."
      }
    ],
    "synthesis_rationale": "Starting from a 5% anchor, the net effect of the factors is predominantly downward due to the large margin and legal thresholds, with modest upward pressure from petition activity and potential delays. The combination yields a calibrated posterior near 1%, acknowledging correlated effects and the historically rare nature of overturns. Calibration accounts for potential over- or under-estimation by weighting by factor strength and known precedents."
  }
}

